From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:32:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] selftests: apple-dcp: stub the m4 HDR atomic check in
 the VRR unit

The vrr-rejection host unit extracts dcp_crtc_atomic_check() from dcp.c
and compiles it against local stubs. "drm/apple: m4: show HDR content as
EDR on the J604 panel (opt-in)" adds an iomfb_m4_atomic_check_hdr() call
to the m4 branch of that function, which the unit does not declare, so
the unit stopped compiling (-Werror=implicit-function-declaration) and
the test reported "not ok".

Stub it like the other m4 helpers the unit already stubs: iomfb_is_m4()
is false in this unit, so the m4 branch must never be reached and the
stub asserts.

[j604: integration fix for linux-aurora 1.608: the ports
 harness update makes vrr-rejection pass (base 27 ok / 30 not ok -> 30 / 27) and
 the DCP EDR commit adds the call; neither branch had both. No
 kernel code change.]

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
(cherry picked from commit 1f20dc769c85393f34b0a2c3724600cc43960422)
---
 tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py b/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py
index f42f8251fe..76dbdc6f01 100644
--- a/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py
+++ b/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py
@@ -1800,6 +1800,9 @@ static bool iomfb_is_m4(struct apple_dcp *d) { (void)d; return false; }
 static int iomfb_m4_error(struct apple_dcp *d) { (void)d; assert(false); return -ENODEV; }
 static int iomfb_m4_get_mode(struct apple_dcp *d,struct drm_display_mode *m)
 { (void)d; (void)m; assert(false); return -ENODEV; }
+static int iomfb_m4_atomic_check_hdr(struct apple_dcp *d, struct drm_crtc *c,
+    struct drm_atomic_commit *s)
+{ (void)d; (void)c; (void)s; assert(false); return -ENODEV; }
 static unsigned drm_plane_mask(void *p) { (void)p; assert(false); return 0; }
 static bool drm_mode_equal(const struct drm_display_mode *a,const struct drm_display_mode *b)
 { (void)a; (void)b; assert(false); return false; }
